=circuit.positive_input&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&view=arguments&node=circuit.positive_input&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fnodes%2Fcircuit.positive_input","record":{"assumption_ids":[],"boundary":"This is the alternative branch’s explicitly imported external input family. It does not use the zero-temperature full-support theorem. The ordered-Gaussian normalization and mean-zero diagonal correction are fixed before applying the external result. The Lopatto theorem is source-reported here, not independently proved.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-positive-input","lopatto2026_interval_support"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.positive_input","kind":"assumption","label":"Independent finite-temperature input family","locator":"07-positive-temperature.tex:3–129; eq:positive-parisi-pde, eq:positive-parisi-value, eq:positive-parisi-diffusion","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-positive","statement":"For every fixed β₀>1, import the finite-temperature Parisi formula and a minimizing Parisi measure μ_{β₀} with support [0,q_{β₀}], q_{β₀}<1, from the stated interval-support result. With γ=β₀μ([0,t]), terminal β₀^(−1)log(2cosh(β₀x)), m=Φ_x and a=Φ_xx, import the bounded-strip regularity, diffusion and contact identity E[m(t,X_t)²]=t for 0≤t≤q_{β₀}, and dm=a dW.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_input","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/circuit.positive_mesh","id":"field:159ea2ed7508b26499539d475f39fd0e27accbac324edfd755f09cd5b87b918f","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef